  "description": "CR 603.3b / 608.2f Nihiloor taps a creature for each opponent at once, and its reflexives go on the stack in the order its controller picks",
  "note": "Nihiloor's ruling: a creature is chosen for each opponent, they are tapped at the same time, and then one reflexive per creature goes on the stack, in the order its controller chooses, beside any trigger the tapping caused. The Merfolk of the Depths (power 4) chosen for bob is no choice for carol, so she gets the Coral Merfolk (power 2). Deeproot Pilgrimage sees one tapping and makes one token. Alice stacks carol's reflexive first, then the Pilgrimage, then bob's. Carol's refuses bob's Ogre and her Hill Giant (power 3) and takes her Bears; bob's refuses the Craw Wurm (power 6) and carol's Lions and takes the Ogre. They resolve top down: the Ogre, then the token, then the Bears.",
